# Double remainder with integer operands

Takes 10.5 modulo 3 in both operand orders to verify the integer is
promoted and the result stays a double, producing 1.5 when the double is
the dividend and 1 when the integer is the dividend.

>>> source
double_value: double = 10.5
integer_divisor: int = 3
integer_dividend: int = 10
double_divisor: double = 3

// Verifies the Int-to-Double promotion with the double dividend first.
double_remainder: double = double_value % integer_divisor
print(double_remainder)

// Verifies the same promotion with the operand order reversed.
integer_remainder: double = integer_dividend % double_divisor
print(integer_remainder)

<<< stdout
1.5
1

<<< stderr
